meta {
  name: Connector Credentials - OAuth Complete
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/connector-credentials/oauth/complete
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "state": "{{oauthState}}",
    "code": "auth-code-123"
  }
}

docs {
  Finishes the OAuth flow `- OAuth Initiate` started. Called by the frontend
  page the provider redirected the member to (`/oauth/connector-complete`),
  with the `state` and `code` from that page's query string.

  Signed in, and only as the member who started the flow: a `state` from
  anyone else is refused (422) and burnt, so a sign-in link can't be used
  to connect someone else's account to your workspace. The member must
  still be allowed to manage connectors in the workspace.

  The workspace comes from the `state` row, so the URL carries none.
  Deletes the `state` row and stores (or reconnects) the credential.

  Response is wrapped (201):
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { connector_credential } }`.
}
